@startuml r19-item-oop-invariant
title OOP-Correct Invariant: EXACTLY-ONCE Listener Registration\nRegardless of Path or Timing

skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<current>> #FFCCCC
  BackgroundColor<<fix>> #CCFFCC
}

package "CURRENT (broken)" <<current>> {
  class "rb-trace-tree\n(renderItems)" as TT_BAD {
    renderItems():
      innerHTML = '' ← NUKE
      for root of items:
        buildSeedNode() ← setAttribute
    --
    ⚠️ Each tree.items= setter
    DESTROYS + RECREATES all items
    ⚠️ buildSeedNode uses setAttribute
    (not .data property)
  }

  class "rb-object-item\n(attribute path)" as ITEM_BAD {
    connectedCallback():
      classList.add() ← cursor
      addEventListener() ← click
      render() ← from getAttribute
    attributeChangedCallback():
      if (!isConnected) return ← SKIP
      render()
    --
    ⚠️ Listener ONLY from connectedCallback
    ⚠️ If connectedCallback never fires
    (plain HTMLElement) → permanently dead
    ⚠️ render() reads attributes which
    may be empty if set before upgrade
  }
}

package "FIX (OOP invariant)" <<fix>> {
  class "rb-trace-tree\n(diff-render)" as TT_FIX {
    renderItems():
      diff existing vs new data
      UPDATE: item.data = newData
      REMOVE: departed.remove()
      APPEND: new item, item.data = d
    --
    ✅ NEVER innerHTML=''
    ✅ Existing items preserved
    ✅ Uses .data property setter
    ✅ New items get .data before append
  }

  class "rb-object-item\n(property path)" as ITEM_FIX {
    private _data: ItemData | null
    private _initialized = false
    --
    set data(d: ItemData):
      _data = d
      if (_initialized) render()
    connectedCallback():
      upgradeProperty('data')
      if (!_initialized):
        _initialized = true
        classList.add('object-item')
        addEventListener('click', handler)
      render() ← from _data field
    disconnectedCallback():
      // DO NOT remove listener
      // DO NOT set _initialized=false
      // Element may be re-appended
    --
    ✅ _initialized guard = EXACTLY-ONCE
    ✅ data stored in field, not attrs
    ✅ connectedCallback always renders
    from field (survives upgrade)
    ✅ Re-append safe (no double-listener)
  }
}

note bottom of TT_FIX
  THE INVARIANT:
  1. Item created ONCE (createElement)
  2. .data set ONCE (property setter stores to field)
  3. Appended ONCE (connectedCallback fires, reads field)
  4. Updated via .data setter (re-renders in place)
  5. NEVER destroyed by innerHTML=''
  6. If re-appended: connectedCallback fires but
     _initialized=true → skip listener add → no double

  ORDER-INDEPENDENT because:
  - .data before append: stored in field, rendered on connect
  - .data after append: rendered immediately (isConnected=true)
  - define() before create: upgraded at createElement
  - define() after create: upgraded at define(), connectedCallback fires
  - All 4 permutations → same result
end note

note bottom of TT_BAD #FFCCCC
  WHY MEMBERS WORK, FILES DON'T:

  MEMBERS: created in ONE batch AFTER
  whenDefined gate (line 231). define() has
  run. createElement returns RbObjectItem.
  connectedCallback fires on appendChild.
  ALWAYS WORKS.

  FILES: FILE_ADDED arrives DURING render()
  await. Each FILE_ADDED sets tree.items =
  [...] which calls renderItems() which does
  innerHTML='' + fresh buildSeedNode.
  Items created BEFORE define() → plain
  HTMLElement. innerHTML='' destroys them
  before define() upgrades them.
  INCONSISTENTLY BROKEN.
end note

@enduml
